// HLZ-005 — './../x' is rejected with a diagnostic that says what to write.
//
// It names the same file as '../x', but the AST records only parent_levels,
// so the two spellings are indistinguishable once parsed: the formatter would
// rewrite one into the other and its token-stream safety gate would refuse the
// file. One canonical spelling, and an error that points at it — the previous
// message was "expected module path" followed by "unexpected token: Slash",
// which named neither the cause nor the fix.
<# ./../shared/lib => s

>> "unreachable" ¶
